{"reference":"Jeremiah 43","book":"Jeremiah","chapter":43,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Wider Setting","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Jeremiah 43 belongs to the book’s extended account of Judah’s crisis under Babylonian domination: deportation, the destruction of Jerusalem, the aftermath associated with Gedaliah, and the flight to Egypt. This wider setting helps locate the chapter’s movement into Egypt within an ongoing narrative of upheaval and displacement rather than as an isolated episode.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_043_d812e3e1d2f70f063c21c98c"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}